# The rpm spec is the reference for anything unexplained here: this file is its translation,
# field for field, into Debian's terms.
Source: hostpinger
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Gleb Romanov <gleb.romanov@outlook.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Homepage: https://github.com/gr584/HostPinger
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: hostpinger
# The staged publish is linux-x64, so the package is not portable to other architectures even
# though most of its content is IL (the spec's ExclusiveArch).
Architecture: amd64
# The application is published framework-dependent, so the runtime is patched by its publisher —
# which on Debian is Microsoft's package repository, since Debian ships no .NET of its own.
# ASP.NET Core rather than just dotnet-runtime: this is a web application. adduser is named
# because postinst calls it and it is Priority: important rather than essential.
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, aspnetcore-runtime-10.0, adduser
Description: Pings configured hosts on a schedule and serves the HostPinger web UI
 HostPinger pings a configured list of hosts on a schedule, records every
 attempt in a local SQLite database, and serves a web UI showing current
 state, response times and downtime history.
 .
 It runs as a systemd service under its own unprivileged account, holding
 only CAP_NET_RAW so that it can send ICMP echo requests.
